     "Not yet. Battery packs (BAT-500) are lithium-cell parts, so Purchase Policy §6.2 applies: they may be bought only from a supplier holding a valid UN 38.3 certificate on file in Ledgerline, uploaded and checked before the first order. Brightcell Energy (Lyon) is not in the supplier master, so it must first be onboarded under SOP-PUR-001: search the master, raise form NBC-F-112 with the quotation, collect the documents, get the purchase manager's approval, create the supplier on PUR-SUP-01, upload its UN 38.3 certificate (type UN38.3, document reference, valid-to) and have the senior buyer check it (checklist NBC-F-113). Since 1 September 2026 (AMD-SUP-2026-02) the report must have been issued within the last 12 months and be valid at least 60 days after the order; Brightcell's report is still being renewed (expected December 2026). Under §6.4 a cheaper quote (Brightcell's £104.00 against £119.00) alone is no reason to change supplier for a lithium-cell part. Ledgerline will not stop the order (PUR.CERT_CHK is N; patch 7.2.3-P4's check is only a warning and is switched off), so the check is yours. Keep ordering from Voltway Cells (VC-EIN-0042) at the contract rate of £119.00 meanwhile.",
     ["F-PUR-6.2", "F-SUP-NOBRIGHT", "F-SOP1-CERT", "F-SOP1-UPLOAD", "F-SOP1-CHECK", "F-AMD2-1.1", "F-PUR-6.4", "F-RNP4-CERT", "F-CAB-031", "F-EM-BRIGHT-PRICE", "F-EM-BRIGHT-CERT", "F-RATE-VC500"],
